  "outstanding": [
    "The isotropic shell count and the compact nonzero-fibre mean are reconstructed in the orbit argument. The Hilbert-plane Möbius action and balanced cusp height floor, the finite-adelic Weil datum, Iwasawa factorization, finite-orbit inverse-denominator decay, and theta and Eisenstein automorphy, and the split-extension parabolic Haar measure and quotient unfolding are supplied by SCR-01, SCR-02, and SCR-03."
  ]
